// wdoc section: Tilemaps.
page wdoc_tilemaps { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Tilemaps"

  p "A `tilemap` draws a 2D grid of indexed tiles cropped from a shared spritesheet. Authored numerically (a list of int rows) or symbolically via a glyph legend."

  h2 "Declaring a tileset"

  p "`tileset` names a spritesheet image plus its slice geometry. The sheet's pixel dimensions are read from the image header at build time (PNG / JPEG / GIF supported); set `image_width`/`image_height` to override."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
tileset platformer {
  source       = "assets/kenney-platformer.png"
  tile_width   = 16
  tile_height  = 16
  // columns, margin, spacing all default sensibly from the image
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Numeric tiles"

  p "Inside a `diagram` (or `container`), a `tilemap` draws cells from the named tileset. `tiles` is a list of int rows; `-1` (the default `empty` index) leaves a cell blank."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width = 320  height = 240
  tilemap {
    set   = "platformer"
    scale = 2.0
    tiles = [
      [ -1, -1,  0,  0, -1, -1 ],
      [ -1,  3,  3,  3,  3, -1 ],
    ]
  }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Symbolic maps"

  p "For map-like authoring, declare a glyph legend with `tile` children and supply `map` (a list of utf8 rows). Unmapped glyphs draw nothing."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
tilemap {
  set = "platformer"
  tile "#" { index = 0 }
  tile "." { index = 3 }
  map = [
    "..##..",
    "..####",
    "######",
  ]
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Scaling"

  p "`scale` sizes the display. `image-rendering: pixelated` is the default (set via the always-injected `TILEMAP_CSS`); `smooth = true` opts into browser smoothing."

  callout "Hosted, not file://" {
    class = ["note"]
    body  = "Tilemaps reference the spritesheet by relative URL, so they only render when served / hosted. wcl wdoc serve handles this locally."
  }

  p "Next: [Dopesheets](wdoc_dopesheets)."
}
